  "answer": "Support should take the following actions for missing or weak citations on scanned PDFs:\n\n1. **Check upload metadata** to see if the file is flagged as an image-only PDF, and confirm that the customer's workspace has OCR enabled [NL-006#NL-006-S03].\n2. **Check if OCR completed without errors** [NL-028#NL-028-S03], and inspect the OCR logs to see if page boundaries were missed during indexing [NL-006#NL-006-S04].\n3. **Inspect the admin logs** for the query to identify the source ID and section ID, verify the source document's status (e.g., not \"deprecated\" or \"stale\"), and confirm the user has permission to view the underlying source [NL-006#NL-006-S04].\n4. **Instruct the customer to inspect the scan quality** and, if possible, export the document directly from the source system as a digital, text-searchable PDF rather than scanning a printed sheet; if scanned files must be used, recommend using the Advanced OCR Pipeline (available to Enterprise customers or as a Growth add-on) for layout-aware reconstruction [NL-006#NL-006-S03].\n5. **If OCR is complete and had no errors**, re-index the folder to refresh vector mappings [NL-028#NL-028-S03].\n\nANSWER_STATUS: answer\nUSED_MEMORY_CLAIMS: none",
